; Manifest-phase family, 6 of 6. An `(alt :keys …)` names `nosuch`, which is
; not a declared key of `route`.
;
; The group's alternatives are key *references*; an unresolvable one makes
; the group's cardinality unenforceable — `at-most-one` over an alternative
; that can never be present degenerates to no constraint at all. Rejecting
; at load is what stops the group from silently weakening.
;
; `exclusive_group_invalid` covers four distinct malformations (fewer than
; two alternatives, an unknown key, naming the discriminant, and a key
; shared across two groups). Only the unknown-key one is pinned here; the
; rest are Zig-side, since a case per malformation would pin the same
; emitter four times.
(plugin :name routes :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name route
    (key :name from :type symbol :optional true)
    (key :name at :type symbol :optional true)
    (exclusive-group :cardinality at-most-one
      (alt :keys [from])
      (alt :keys [nosuch]))))

(route :from a)
